`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The app is two halves joined by a deliberately tiny contract. A native Swift/AppKit shell puts one borderless ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"NSWindow"})," on screen per note, each hosting a ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"WKWebView"}),". The editor inside is CodeMirror 6 with a custom live-preview plugin that hides formatting tokens except on the lines the selection touches. When text, color, or a drag happens, the web view posts a small message; Swift moves windows and writes files. The editor never assumes the bridge exists, so the same page runs headless in a browser, which is what the parity test suite drives."]}),`
