`,e.jsxs(t.p,{children:[e.jsx(t.strong,{children:"Migrated from a hand-rolled editor to CodeMirror 6."})," The first editor was a contenteditable engine; its undo and cross-line selection were the worst defects. Moving to CodeMirror bought native undo, real selection, IME, and a proper Lezer markdown parser, at the cost of learning its decoration and precedence rules. The custom live-preview plugin reproduces the per-line reveal on top of native editing."]}),`
