`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Inference engines like vLLM cache the KV state of recent prompts and reuse it when a new prompt starts the same way. Agents resend the same system prompt and tool definitions every step, and conversations resend their history every turn, so most of a prompt is often already cached somewhere in the pool. A cache-blind load balancer scatters related requests across replicas, and each replica recomputes prefixes another one already holds."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"Switchyard is a router that sits in front of a pool of OpenAI-compatible model servers and sends each request to the replica most likely to have its prefix cached, balanced against load."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.h2,{id:"requirements",children:e.jsx(t.a,{href:"#requirements",children:"Requirements"})}),`
`,e.jsxs(t.ul,{children:[`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Speak the OpenAI API, streaming and non-streaming, and propagate client cancellation to the engine."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Know what each replica has cached without running a tokenizer on the hot path."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Add well under a millisecond of latency per request."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Survive replica failures and restarts without routing to stale beliefs."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.li,{children:"Measure results against named baselines on real hardware, with the method written down before the numbers."}),`
