`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"On the GPU it lost to prefix affinity. The four replicas share one GPU, and the cost model assumed independent compute, so moving a request to an idle replica looked faster when that replica was competing for the same device. I added a shared-accelerator mode to the simulator, which reproduced the GPU result, then tried three device-aware variants of the cost model. None helped, so I reverted them, recorded the attempts in an architecture decision record, and made prefix affinity the default."}),`
