`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"AI Trip Planner is a full-stack application for generating travel itineraries from user preferences and plotting them on a live map. It is intentionally small enough to ship, but it exercises the same boundaries a larger AI product needs: typed UI state, backend-owned model calls, response normalization, latency handling, and deployment."}),`
`,e.jsx(t.p,{children:"The important design choice is that the frontend does not call the model provider directly. The Go API owns prompt construction, inference calls, response shaping, and failure handling. The map is a first-class part of the UI, not an afterthought bolted onto a results list: recommendations render as markers on a MapLibre GL canvas backed by keyless OpenFreeMap tiles."}),`
`,e.jsx(d,{groups:[{title:"Frontend",items:["React","typed form state","MapLibre GL map","itinerary rendering"]},{title:"Backend",items:["Go API","prompt assembly","response normalization"]},{title:"Inference",items:["Groq API","model timeout","fallback messaging"]}],caption:"Model-specific behavior stays behind the API boundary so the UI can render a stable itinerary contract."}),`
